#
# The build context of .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile, the one image built from
# this tree: only what the fuzz build reads. No .git, whose config can hold the
# token of a clone, no target directory, and nothing else a development
# checkout keeps. It sits at the root, not beside the Dockerfile, because only
# BuildKit reads a Dockerfile-specific ignore file: a docker CLI without
# buildx, such as that of Ubuntu's docker.io package, which OSS-Fuzz's helper
# may run, still uses the legacy builder.
*
!.cargo/
!.clusterfuzzlite/
!Cargo.lock
!Cargo.toml
!rust-toolchain.toml
!nails-*/
!fuzz/
**/target/
fuzz/artifacts/
fuzz/corpus/
fuzz/coverage/
